# A) Undoing local uncommitted changes

1. undoing the local changes that has not been committed yet

---

    git restore <file_name>

---

2. restoring deleted file

---

    git restore <file_name>

---

3. to view changes in a file

---

    git diff <file_name>

---

# B) Undoing local committed changes

1. Fixing the last commit ( using amend)

2. Using git revert( it doesnt change the old commit hostory)

---

git revert <commit-hash>

//it will revert only those changes introduced by the commit, if merge conflicts ,will ask to resolve

---

3. using git reset( to remove some coomits as if they never were made, excluding the hash of commit we use)

---

## git reset --hard <commit-hash>

4. Reseting a file to an old version

---

     git restore --source <hash-of-coomit> <file_name>

